---
term: Amendment threshold
section: evolution-and-protection
order: 80
definition: The level of member support required to change a particular part of a charter.
example: A charter lets a simple majority revise quarterly targets. Changing the exit procedure requires two-thirds support in two votes held at least six months apart.
seeAlso:
  - amendment
  - fundamental-protections
---
Thresholds rise with each deeper [[tiered constitutional design|constitutional layer]]. Operational provisions change easily so that the corporation can adapt quickly. Fundamental protections change only with broad, sustained support.

The difference in speed is deliberate. An executive that adapts quickly within a charter that changes slowly can't use its speed to rewrite its own constraints, and neither can a faction that wins a single vote.
